From 97dee3dc3d3147c59038454d9b37271e7fac7d77 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shaun Adams <s.adams@f5.com>
Date: Mon, 15 Jun 2026 08:56:40 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 33/42] ui+transports: multi-tenant tenant picker, badge,
 switcher, and URL rewriter
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Stage 1 + Stage 2 of the multi-tenant UI rollout in one patch
because Stage 1's tenant-context plumbing is unobservable without
Stage 2's URL rewriter: with just the picker, every admin call still
hit the legacy /api/* paths and showed the default tenant's data.

Backend:
- GET /api/session/tenants — public, minimal {id, name, status} tenant
  directory powering the login picker. Whitelisted from the auth
  middleware so it's reachable BEFORE the user has credentials. Full
  per-tenant metadata + write ops stay behind auth on
  /api/platform/tenants.

Redux state:
- tenantSlice: currentTenantID + setCurrentTenant/clearTenant actions
  that persist to localStorage so a hard reload keeps the same tenant.
- useCurrentTenant hook — canonical accessor for components.
- store.ts wires the reducer + a createListenerMiddleware that
  dispatches baseApi.util.invalidateTags(<every tenant-scoped tag>)
  on every setCurrentTenant/clearTenant. Without invalidation,
  RTK Query keeps serving the previous tenant's cached data even
  though the URL the baseQuery would now hit is different (cache key
  is the JS arg, not the URL).

RTK Query baseQuery:
- TENANT_SCOPED_PREFIXES (= /providers, /governance/{virtual-keys,
  teams,customers,budgets,rate-limits}, /mcp/clients): URLs in these
  prefixes are rewritten to /tenants/{tid}/... when a tenant is
  active. Endpoint definitions across the 30+ admin API files stay
  agnostic — single source of truth for tenant scoping.
- New "Tenants" cache tag.
- tenantsApi: getTenantsPublic (login picker, public endpoint),
  getTenants/getTenant/createTenant (admin, in-workspace switcher).

UI:
- loginView: tenant dropdown (queries getTenantsPublic), with a
  "+ New tenant…" sentinel that flips into two inputs (id+name) and
  on Sign in does login → POST /api/platform/tenants → setCurrentTenant
  → navigate, all in one click. 409 = activate existing.
- TenantBadge component (top-right of workspace shell): shows the
  active tenant's name + caret, opens a dropdown listing every
  tenant (admin endpoint) for switching. Persists across navigation.
- clientLayout mounts the badge above main.

Ref: https://jira.f5net.com/browse/XC-25496
